  "_exec_summary": [
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 0,
      "FacilityID": 1000120462,
      "SummaryText": "Kinder Morgan Liquids Terminals, LLC (KMLT) - Galena Park is a refined petroleum products and chemicals bulk storage and distribution facility. This Risk Management Plan (RMP) specifically applies to the Butane Truck Loading and Unloading Process which includes two dual purpose truck unloading/loading stations. The stations are connected to a DOT regulated breakout tank and butane is supplied to the stations using DOT regulated transfer equipment.\n\nThe Butane Truck Loading and Unloading Process was constructed in accordance with the National Fire Protection Association (NFPA Code) No. 58 (2024 Edition) for Liquefied Petroleum Gas Storage. KMLT maintains and operates the process in accordance with NFPA No. 58 and the manufacturers' instructions and recommendations. It is the policy of KMLT to adhere to all applicable federal, state, and local laws/codes. In addition, KMLT complies with the U.S. Environmental Protection Agency's (EPA) Accident Prevention Rules (40 CFR Part 68 Subpart D) and the Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) Process Safety Management (PSM) standard and associated 14 elements (29 CFR Part 1910.119).\n\nThe facility has developed and maintains an Emergency Response Action Plan. The plan is coordinated annually at minimum with local responders and training activities occur periodically. In the event of an emergency involving the Butane Truck Loading and Unloading Process, it is KMLT's policy to initially contact the local fire department through the 911 service.\n\nAs this is an initial submittal and the Butane Truck Loading and Unloading Process has not begun operations, this facility has not had an accident involving the Butane Truck Loading and Unloading Process which has resulted in deaths, injuries, property/environmental damage, evacuations, or sheltering in place.\n\nKMLT actively seeks employee input on process safety improvements. Additionally, local emergency responders are contacted periodically regarding participation in site"
    },
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 1,
      "FacilityID": 1000120462,
      "SummaryText": "emergency response drills. Additional actions include consolidating separate system inspection checklists for ease of completion."
    }
  ]
